            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and evaluation of a 2-benzothiazolylphenylmethyl ether class of histamine H4 receptor antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5263-5266</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(16)30991-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2016.09.049</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synthesis and biological evaluation of a new class of histamine H4 receptor ligands, distinct from the previously reported chemotypes, are described. A virtual screening of our corporate compound collection identified a hit with an undesired dual H3R/H4R activity. Chemical exploration led to the discovery of a more potent and selective 2-benzothiazolylphenylmethyl ether lead compound.</AbstractText>
